{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse","id":1374626,"title":"Giving the Unconquerable Sun an excuse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-13T13:21:38-07:00","id":1374626,"title":"Giving the Unconquerable Sun an excuse","content":"What would it change, if it were made canon that the Unconquered Sun KNEW about the Great Contagion and the Fair Folk Invasion, and the reason he didn't step in and do anything is because he'd given Creation to Exalted and humanity in general as a reward for their service in the Primordial War?<br /> <br /> What if the only way he could intervene would be to break his promise? Which would, if he's anything like his Late Second Edition self, would actually render him vulnerable.<br /> <br /> Or, what if there was an &quot;escape clause&quot; that would allow the Unconquered Sun to step in, but only if he determined that Creation was about to be completely destroyed, and that the Exalted and humanity had therefore broken their end of the agreement. By proving themselves unreliable to manage and protect Creation, he gained the legal right to take back control of it, turning all of humanity back into a subject species.<br /> <br /> Keeping in mind that, at the time, he'd already turned his back on humanity. He doesn't have to fear a revolt of the Solar Exalted Host if he doesn't Chose any more of them.<br /> <br /> In the end, the Exalted DID save Creation (via the Scarlet Empress), so the Unconquered Sun went back to the Games of Divinity, assured that the Exalted could be allowed to command Creation for at least a little while longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T14:23:06-07:00","id":1374634,"title":"","content":"What would it change if he knew? I think it would add a 'proud, benevolent father' spin to the worst loss of life since the Time of Glory. <br /> <br /> He, being the chief war god, and they, being the Fair Folk, his most familiar enemy, I think it is possible he had the measure of the war before it began. <br /> <br /> As for escape clauses, I do not see the Sun using them, or even thinking to create them. He would keep his promise even if it meant going down with the ship. Because he could not foresee any circumstance where the choice he made, no matter how long ago, was not the right course of action. Rather, he'd have to be convinced by Luna to change his mind, or by the Maidens of other promises of his that he would break to his godly subjects through inaction, to consider intervening in Creation. They are a team, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T14:33:41-07:00","id":1374635,"title":"","content":"The general thing to me is that he doesn't need one. He could just have simply thought the Exalted could handle it (they in the end did). I think that often the &quot;Why didn't he Sun do anything?&quot; or &quot;Why didn't the Contagion just make the Solars necessary afterall?&quot; kind of have usntated assumptions that either the Sun or his Chosen were omnipotent enough that the Contagion and subsequent invasion were things they'd trivially stop.<br /> <br /> Nothing like the Balorian Crusade ever happened before. Nothing like it will probably ever happen again. He might have even Exalted the Solars he could at the time as an act. I think that a lot of these discussions kind of assume Active Sun = World Saved. It's something that even with his experience in the past is not necessarily the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T17:33:58-07:00","id":1374661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374635#post1374635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The general thing to me is that he doesn't need one. He could just have simply thought the Exalted could handle it (they in the end did). I think that often the &quot;Why didn't he Sun do anything?&quot; or &quot;Why didn't the Contagion just make the Solars necessary afterall?&quot; kind of have usntated assumptions that either the Sun or his Chosen were omnipotent enough that the Contagion and subsequent invasion were things they'd trivially stop.<br /> <br /> Nothing like the Balorian Crusade ever happened before. Nothing like it will probably ever happen again. He might have even Exalted the Solars he could at the time as an act. I think that a lot of these discussions kind of assume Active Sun = World Saved. It's something that even with his experience in the past is not necessarily the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it helps we can try to make things more specific.<br /> <br /> One thing he could have done was lead a mortal to the Realm Defense Grid / Sword of Creation. Presumably this would have worked earlier, because it worked when the Empress did it. Presumably he didn't actually do this, because he would have lead a Solar and not a Solar-hating Dragonblooded. He can pass some information to solars - specifically to Zeniths, when they Exalt.<br /> <br /> But obviously there are many possible reasons he didn't do that. Either he didn't know about its existence, or he didn't know enough information about it to be helpful to seekers, or the Sword of Creation specifically had a special place in the &quot;you guys are in charge of this&quot; deal, or he did actually tell someone but it failed for another reason, or...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T07:37:30-07:00","id":1374754,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like the interpretation of Creation where the Celestial Incarnae are flawed to varying degrees, and none more so than the Unconquered Sun, King of All the Gods. The fact that He didn't do anything during the Great Contagion or the Balorian Crusade fits beautifully into that narrative.<br /> <br /> In my interpretation, the King of All the Gods fought a war to gain the Games of Divinity (or was corrupted when the Primordials allowed Him to make a single move there, a successful strategy to break Him) and bestowed the Creation-Ruling Mandate in order to play Games full time. When the Solars proved villainous, He preferred a symbolic condemnation - turning His back on Creation (and toward the Games) - to actually intervening or even descending to demand that His Chosen shape up. Possibly He still cared enough to feel grief at the Lawgivers' betrayal, but if He did it only served to drive Him further into escaping heartbreak in the Games. By the time of the Contagion/Crusade, it was pretty hard for anyone in Yu-Shan to divert His attention even momentarily.<br /> <br /> I prefer that interpretation in a vaccum because I like the undercurrent of horror in &quot;what if the Gods are awful?&quot; I also prefer distant, apathetic Gods because it puts the focus back on the player characters. But I also think it fits the history of Exalted better. Considerable mental gymnastics are necessary to reconcile &quot;The Unconquered Sun is righteous&quot; and &quot;The Unconquered Sun sat back and watched Creation die.&quot;<br /> <br /> I thought the write-up of the Unconquered Sun in Glories of the Most High was a bit silly. Even if I wanted to run the Unconquered Sun as righteous and glorious, the idea that he's engaging in some philosophical sophistry that ends up with him sticking his head in the sand so he doesn't have to engage with difficult real-world situations that would force him to compromise his perfect virtue seems a bit pathetic. Surely that evasive crap is also a compromise of virtue. A noble casting of the Unconquered Sun, who can be weakened by moral compromises, suggests a story where he <i>does</i> descend, <i>does</i> get involved in Terrestrial affairs, and ends up vulnerable and weakened as a result. Maybe that leads to a story where the PCs have to save their God. Maybe it leads to a story where the Unconquered Sun dies. That could be interesting too.<br /> <br /> tl;dr Don't give Him an excuse. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T09:18:43-07:00","id":1374767,"title":"","content":"Okay I might need to ask : Is there a canonical simple answer of what the Sun has been doing during the Time of Tumult and until now, and is there an explanation for why he decided to come back to Creation ? Was there no Solar on Creation during so long because he didn't care or because of the mystical Jade Prisons I've heard about ? Or do we know nothing for the moment and it's all up to interpretation ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T11:46:05-07:00","id":1374779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374767#post1374767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay I might need to ask : Is there a canonical simple answer of what the Sun has been doing during the Time of Tumult and until now, and is there an explanation for why he decided to come back to Creation ? Was there no Solar on Creation during so long because he didn't care or because of the mystical Jade Prisons I've heard about ? Or do we know nothing for the moment and it's all up to interpretation ?</div> </div> </div> </div>3e seems pretty explicit that the Jade Prison is responsible for the lack of solars:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3E Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Most of the Solars were murdered and their Essences sealed away in a jade prison\u2014for such was their power </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">that they could reincarnate upon death.<br /> <br /> ...</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">the doors of the </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">jade prison have been kicked open, and the heroes of old have come again. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>But there weren't no solars, there were the few that escaped the Jade Prison, endlessly reincarnating and getting hunted down.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun turned his back on creation at the height of the First Age (which I think was supposed to be well before all the Solars got locked in the Prison) but turns his face now - I think this is supposed to be caused by the Solar's return, and not vice versa.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3E Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">At the height of the </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\"><i>First </i></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\"><i>Age</i></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">, he turned his face from </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\"><i>Creation </i></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">in anger at the excesses of the Solars.<br /> <br /> ....</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">It is known in Heaven that some great blasphemy by the Exalted of the First </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Age made him wroth, and so he </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">turned his face from the world. Now </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">he turns it back</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since the Usurpation, a few things we know the Unconquered Sun has been doing are:<ul><li>Exalting new Solars after old ones die</li> <li>Talking to Zeniths when he Exalts them</li> <li>Helping other gods create Exigents</li> </ul>As far as I know, that's everything that's canon, and everything else is up to the storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T12:27:28-07:00","id":1374784,"title":"","content":"Okay so we don't know exactly why he changed his mind ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T12:39:21-07:00","id":1374787,"title":"","content":"I've always seen his lack of action to be a mix of depression and <i>not</i> being perfect. He's not a omnibenevolent god, nor is he omnipotent. He's more supposed to be Jupiter than Jehovah.<br /> <br /> But if you want to have a completely good UCS Sunder, I guess you could go with that Christian reasoning. It could work. He wanted to help, but couldn't, being trapped by his own principles and promises.<br /> <br /> <br /> In my previous game, the UCS actually... vanished mysteriously. Possibly killed. As did Luna. Now Heaven is ruled by Autocthon, and five gods pretending to be the Maidens (Siakel is impersonating Mars, but I don't know who the others are).<br /> <br /> Anyway, no need to explain how the UCS can act imperfectly if he's just gone.<br /> <br /> In my current game... well, who knows. There's a distant sun god. The Solars were first seen literally last session (session 16), they said they'd escaped from Hell where they'd been trapped by the Dragons. And it's been suggested that they stole the UCS's power thousands of years ago, becoming Solars, so he may not even be involved in Exalting them. Who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T14:02:14-07:00","id":1374798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374784#post1374784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so we don't know exactly why he changed his mind ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, no.<br /> <br /> I went through every mention of the word &quot;Unconquered&quot; in the 3E core book to make that post, so I'm pretty sure it's not in there.<br /> <br /> For me, the obvious simplest explanation that leaps out from the text is something like &quot;The original solars of the First Age did bad stuff, and kept doing it, until the Usurpation. Afterwards, there were so few Solars, and so weak, that he didn't feel like they had a chance to redeem themselves. Now, with the full might of the Solars returned, he is hopeful that they can do better.&quot; This is a pretty natural extrapolation of what we were given that puts agency in the hands of the players but gives Sol Invictus a little room to show up.<br /> <br /> Another interesting possibility to explore would be that it's really the creation of the Abyssals and Infernals that gave him a different point of view. Possibly he merely now looks on the Solars more favorably by comparison, or he is trying to manipulate events so that the Abyssals and Infernals can be redeemed. (A minimalist version of that would be that turning his face towards the world consisted precisely of creating some way for the Abyssals to potentially be redeemed.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T14:07:10-07:00","id":1374800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>habitableexoplanet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374798#post1374798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think so, no.Afterwards, there were so few Solars, and so weak</div> </div> </div> </div>Something I was discussing with a friend the other day; does 3rd ed ever mention or suggest that there were Solars at all during the Shogunate and in the 2nd Age prior to recently?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T14:47:42-07:00","id":1374811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374800#post1374800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Something I was discussing with a friend the other day; does 3rd ed ever mention or suggest that there were Solars at all during the Shogunate and in the 2nd Age prior to recently?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is unambiguous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3E Core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">The Sidereals kept a close watch for the few Solars who continued to be reborn into the world. With powerful as</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">trology and mystical instruments of detection, the Sidereals </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">guided armed strike forces of Dragon-Blooded to destroy newly emergent Solars before they had a chance to gain power. Such groups came to be called the Wyld Hunt, and </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">their inquisitions became inseparable from the Immaculate religion. For centuries, the Wyld Hunt rode down, captured </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">and slaughtered the Solar Exalted with impunity. </span></div> </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25834-habitableexoplanet","name":"habitableexoplanet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"296"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T15:46:14-07:00","id":1374822,"title":"","content":"Ah, sure. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T17:10:32-07:00","id":1374835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse#post1374626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would it change, if it were made canon that the Unconquered Sun KNEW about the Great Contagion and the Fair Folk Invasion, and the reason he didn't step in and do anything is because he'd given Creation to Exalted and humanity in general as a reward for their service in the Primordial War?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think much in practical terms, but it kind of cuts away a lot of versatility to how one might approach the character in games if it comes up. And I think focusing into a space of the moral questions raised by that stance might be... contentious in a way that games might be better off without.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the only way he could intervene would be to break his promise? Which would, if he's anything like his Late Second Edition self, would actually render him vulnerable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then he's being characterised as a bit of your Cu Chuliann hero type whose standards for honourable conflict can leave him caught between irreconcilable positions. It wouldn't be unfitting. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, what if there was an &quot;escape clause&quot; that would allow the Unconquered Sun to step in, but only if he determined that Creation was about to be completely destroyed, and that the Exalted and humanity had therefore broken their end of the agreement. By proving themselves unreliable to manage and protect Creation, he gained the legal right to take back control of it, turning all of humanity back into a subject species.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems like a decent source of tension of one wants to present the Unconquered Sun as a presence that looms over the conduct of characters in a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He doesn't have to fear a revolt of the Solar Exalted Host if he doesn't Chose any more of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, at this exact moment I find myself thinking that the whole idea that gods can withhold their Exalted like this to open so many cans of worms, and am not entirely satisfied with some premises of inherent motive that keeps going inevitably, that I'm tempted to headcanon that a kind of caveat of the Law of Diminishment is that the part of yourself that you sacrifice is kind of intertwined with uncapping the will to ever not Choose somebody.<br /> <br /> That's not exactly in the form of &quot;you don't get a choice anymore&quot; as &quot;the commitment to create Exalted is powerful enough that anybody capable of making that step will be invested enough to not just give up on it&quot;.<br /> <br /> Although I don't know, maybe that does ultimately amount to them not getting a choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T18:30:02-07:00","id":1374850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse#post1374626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He doesn't have to fear a revolt of the Solar Exalted Host if he doesn't Chose any more of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Sol literally can't keep from exalting people, even if he actively doesn't want to. Otherwise the Primordials could have just ordered him to stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T19:07:04-07:00","id":1374855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374850#post1374850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure Sol literally can't keep from exalting people, even if he actively doesn't want to. Otherwise the Primordials could have just ordered him to stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was a Second Edition idea, wasn\u2019t it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T19:38:45-07:00","id":1374866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374855#post1374855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was a Second Edition idea, wasn\u2019t it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think (and this is as a latecomer to the setting who has been doing alot of catch up reading) that in 2nd edition, the process of exaltation was largely autonomous. The Exaltation itself zipped to the next worthy individual with little to no involvement from Sol Invictus. I imagine this was established to answer the question of why didn't the Primordials simply command their servants to stop exalting people.<br /> <br /> In third edition, they reframed the question a bit by saying that the Gods did not have to obey the Primordials in all things, so they had the ability to refuse a command to stop creating Exalted,and made the process of Exalting an act of divine will so singular that the Gods would not be able to stop exalting people even if they wanted to. I suspect this was changed in order to make the Exalt's feel more like they were deemed worthy by the Most High directly, rather than chosen by a divine answering service.<br /> <br /> Milage May Vary as to which of these takes is better for your game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T21:25:56-07:00","id":1374874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374855#post1374855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was a Second Edition idea, wasn\u2019t it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. In the 2e Lunars corebook, page 20, there's a quote that implies the god's geas is quite broad:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Primordials could have simply commanded the gods to order their Exalted to surrender </div> </div> </div>Which you could take to mean the Primordials could have ordered the Incarna to stop the process of Exaltation if it was within their power. Obviously, Exigents of the post-Primordial War era could be designed without this at-the-time necessary feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T23:08:32-07:00","id":1374881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374787#post1374787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always seen his lack of action to be a mix of depression and <i>not</i> being perfect. He's not a omnibenevolent god, nor is he omnipotent. He's more supposed to be Jupiter than Jehovah. ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that's my take too. That he even Exalted folks at all in the interrum with what Exaltations he had to me kind of even feeds into that kind of narrative. He hates his Chosen betrayed him in his view, but well, he still likes them and the people who can become them enough that he keeps coming back. To me that his reluctance to do more than that being a combination of stubbornness as well as limits is something I think is a good case.<br /> <br /> And yeah, folks get a bit overly into the Abrahamic god take on him than I think is warranted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T23:13:49-07:00","id":1374882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374855#post1374855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was a Second Edition idea, wasn\u2019t it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is. It's built on the assumption the Primordials had the abiltiy to give orders to the Incarna they couldn't refuse. 3e goes more to the 1e take: The Incarna just couldn't attack their creators. They didn't have to listen to them though. It's just that until they had the Exalted, they couldn't start shit or defend against. When they got their mistletoe, they could well have just told the enemies of the gods to piss off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T23:15:07-07:00","id":1374883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374874#post1374874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. In the 2e Lunars corebook, page 20, there's a quote that implies the god's geas is quite broad:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which you could take to mean the Primordials could have ordered the Incarna to stop the process of Exaltation if it was within their power. Obviously, Exigents of the post-Primordial War era could be designed without this at-the-time necessary feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively 3e just doesn't assume the gods can be ordered to do that and it kind of cutes out a lot of the logic trying ot justify why it wasn't. &quot;Couldn't the Primordials have told them to stop?&quot; can just be answered, &quot;No, they couldn't.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T01:49:28-07:00","id":1374892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryphon's Feather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374850#post1374850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure Sol literally can't keep from exalting people, even if he actively doesn't want to. Otherwise the Primordials could have just ordered him to stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Hey, stop that!&quot;<br /> &quot;Sorry, can't do it.&quot; {smug}<br /> &quot;Fine, start killin' 'em all.&quot;<br /> &quot;Aww snap, always one step ahead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T02:40:15-07:00","id":1374895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374892#post1374892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Hey, stop that!&quot;<br /> &quot;Sorry, can't do it.&quot; {smug}<br /> &quot;Fine, start killin' 'em all.&quot;<br /> &quot;Aww snap, always one step ahead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, according to statline, the Unconquered Sun is pretty fucking horrifying to fight. At least for 2e. <br /> <br /> Unless they were laughing and mocking him for thinking that such a thing would work, until Primordials started dying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T04:08:11-07:00","id":1374901,"title":"","content":"I don't think any of the up-thread suggestions are bad. <br /> <br /> That said, my own, very acanonical, preference is to think that the Mandate of Heaven and perhaps the consequences of banishing the Primordials required a sort of metaphysical distancing of the Sun's power to act in the world to avoid destabilizing Creation. And really that the Incarna as a whole, though particularly the Sun, as the Maidens have their excuses. The Sun must work through the Great Chain of Being of his divine bureaucracy, and his bureaucracy is sometimes unstable and unresponsive to his dictates, particularly when its earthly counterpart is thrown into disarray by disasters like the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> Perhaps slight difference in emphasis in that this is less tied up in his active, current, deeply held principles (&quot;He's so morally committed to the Exalted's stewardship of the world!&quot;) or vices (&quot;He cannot forgive the Exalted and cannot leave the Games of Divinity!&quot;), and his own personal survival. That IMO has an advantage of allows players to potentially interact with the Sun as a distant moral &quot;blank canvas&quot; without leading to questions of his intervention in the world that undermine the thesis of the centrality of human heroism. It leans into the idea that the effective way to work with the Sun is directly through the Celestial Bureaucracy, and supports it as a setting element, in place of players wondering why they don't just show up and make direct appeals to him, and have him intervene directly.<br /> <br /> I do think this is definitely a fundamental setting issue that could do with some thought by anyone working on the setting on a fundamental level, although whether its a good idea to ever nail it down in black-and-white IDK.<br /> <br /> Another possibility I like almost as much is that the Maidens had already told the Sun how it would work out, and he didn't have enough of a problem with that scenario to go against it, perhaps because he saw that interventions by him would cause something worse, like a vast three-way war between the Exalted, Heaven and the Fair Folk, with Hell and the Dead seizing on the opportunity etc. The Sun is enormously excellent and thus we can guess pretty good at strategic prediction himself, and has the benefit of his Circle being quite literally the best seeing the future, themselves.<br /> <br /> Either way I would personally be careful of necessarily tying it to elements of characterization in moral or principles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T06:22:03-07:00","id":1374910,"title":"","content":"What I have the most difficulty finding is why he came back. I usually have no problem headcanoning these kind of things but I really have no idea for why he decided to care again for Creation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T07:17:13-07:00","id":1374917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374910#post1374910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I have the most difficulty finding is why he came back. I usually have no problem headcanoning these kind of things but I really have no idea for why he decided to care again for Creation</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that he cared about Creation.<br /> Then the Solars ruined Creation and he turned his face away.<br /> Then the Usurpation happened and the majority of Solars were locked away in the Jade Prison.<br /> Sol then decides to give the Deebs a shot at running Creation, but still sporadically Exalted Solars and Exigents in extreme circumstances.<br /> Then the Jade Prison was opened and <i>this</i> caused Sol to turn his face back to Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T08:32:53-07:00","id":1374925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374917#post1374917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that he cared about Creation.<br /> Then the Solars ruined Creation and he turned his face away.<br /> Then the Usurpation happened and the majority of Solars were locked away in the Jade Prison.<br /> Sol then decides to give the Deebs a shot at running Creation, but still sporadically Exalted Solars and Exigents in extreme circumstances.<br /> Then the Jade Prison was opened and <i>this</i> caused Sol to turn his face back to Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but his talk when Exalting Perfect Soul seems to be like &quot;Okay I'm back because I like you&quot; but his last thing with Solars was that he was let down by them. I mean the answer could just be &quot;He mourned enough and now he's ready to go&quot; which would make sense as well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T09:09:09-07:00","id":1374931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374925#post1374925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but his last thing with Solars was that he was let down by them. I mean the answer could just be &quot;He mourned enough and now he's ready to go&quot; which would make sense as well</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, a thousand or more years have passed since then, it could very well be that he's come around again. Or maybe Luna convinced him to get back out there and give it another shot - sure, he's been burned before, but maybe those three hundred special someones out there <i>this</i> time won't let him down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T10:36:51-07:00","id":1374938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1374925#post1374925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes but his talk when Exalting Perfect Soul seems to be like &quot;Okay I'm back because I like you&quot; but his last thing with Solars was that he was let down by them. I mean the answer could just be &quot;He mourned enough and now he's ready to go&quot; which would make sense as well</div> </div> </div> </div>In his talk with Perfect Soul, he speaks of turning his face away. This, from other sources, is because of the Solars in the First Age.<br /> <br /> When he turned away, I doubt he anticipated the Usurpation. 1E states that he basically turned a blind eye to the Usurpation figuring the Dragon-Blooded couldn't well do any worse than the Solars.<br /> <br /> Then consider what happened: his chosen were hunted, his worship driven to obscurity, the Great Contagion. It's conceivable that Sol realized he made a mistake... but without his chosen he has no reason to turn his face back to Creation. He turned away, this is what happened.<br /> <br /> But the Jade Prison opening gives Sol the means to meddle in the world of men again. It's a second chance. It's not one Sol has to take, he could have kept his face turned from the world... but he's chosen to turn back and use what he has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T12:39:48-07:00","id":1374959,"title":"","content":"A way to look at it is that after fifteen centuries or more, he's decided to give this another shot. Whether or not he gets burned for it is another matter. But I have this &quot;I'm giving you all another shot&quot; vibe to this. It doens't really need much more than that since he's in the end a person and people decide to do that short of thing or not all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T17:33:46-07:00","id":1375183,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Jade Prison and whatever aspect of their patrons is involved in choosing the Exalted: How did it work exactly? Was the Jade Prison sufficiently powerful to actively resist the Sun's desire to Chose beyond the free Exaltations, did it hide them from his (presumably extremely keen) sight, did it actually stuff in the fates of exceptional mortals so only the barest few were impressive enough to catch his attention, etc.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T18:27:31-07:00","id":1375195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375183#post1375183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How did it work <b>exactly?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably not likely to be explored overmuch in this edition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T19:44:39-07:00","id":1375209,"title":"","content":"I first got into exalted in 2e, but I'm increasingly happy with 3e's treatment of things. Especially in making the exaltation less of a concrete thing. Not expecting an official answer, if you want to headcanon one, go ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Currently Playing:</b> <i>A large, mixed splat game of <b>CofD</b>.</i> <b>As:</b> Seraph du Salomon, Voice on the concordance. Unsubtle man reluctantly participating in the business of Magi. Awakening 2E homebrew <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1338514-house-du-salomon-a-proximus-dynasty?_=1569864567692\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...=1569864567692</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2598-gryphon-s-feather","name":"Gryphon's Feather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2598_3.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"215"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T00:11:29-07:00","id":1375231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375183#post1375183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the Jade Prison and whatever aspect of their patrons is involved in choosing the Exalted: How did it work exactly? Was the Jade Prison sufficiently powerful to actively resist the Sun's desire to Chose beyond the free Exaltations, did it hide them from his (presumably extremely keen) sight, did it actually stuff in the fates of exceptional mortals so only the barest few were impressive enough to catch his attention, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't expect 3E to go into detail. Like how the Primordial War is never mentioned by name but clearly still happened. I imagine that the lore around the Jade Prison will stay the same -- it's a big block of jade cast into the ocean that traps Solar Exaltations, which the Yozi broke open and stole half of the Exaltations, giving 100 to the Deathlords. It just won't ever be talked about in those terms explicitly -- just referenced obliquely. Sol couldn't just make more Exaltations because of the Law of Diminishment, and he had no desire to after seeing what the Solars did to Creation.<br /> <br /> But now he's been given a second chance, as Deathknights blight the land with a dark and twisted spark of his power, in a world lavished by the Contagion and diminished by the Terrestrials, with no Empress to bring law. Sol likely sees the Time of Tulmult as an oppertunity, and a duty, and a penance (for both himself and his Chosen).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T00:46:45-07:00","id":1375234,"title":"","content":"Primordials aren't mentioned, but the war is. It's been called War of the Gods and the Divine Revolution in a few spots. It's name is just focused on well, the winners more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T06:01:04-07:00","id":1375270,"title":"","content":"I think a side consequence of the idea that the Unconquered Sun would have ultimately stepped in to intervene is that it weakens the significance of the Scarlet Empress saving the world and what she went through to acquire that power. Not gone entirely, sure, but the idea that there was a safety net definitely feels like it diminishes the stakes and consequences. I think that also has implications for how to handle big threats that one might want to introduce in their own game of they're working off an actual text of &quot;there's a point at which the most powerful god will step in&quot;.<br /> <br /> Although sure, that does get into the usual issue of how to include somebody like the Sun in the setting while still having stakes. Maybe we'll talk about that a bit later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T08:45:02-07:00","id":1375285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375195#post1375195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably not likely to be explored overmuch in this edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375231#post1375231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't expect 3E to go into detail. Like how the Primordial War is never mentioned by name but clearly still happened. I imagine that the lore around the Jade Prison will stay the same -- it's a big block of jade cast into the ocean that traps Solar Exaltations, which the Yozi broke open and stole half of the Exaltations, giving 100 to the Deathlords. It just won't ever be talked about in those terms explicitly -- just referenced obliquely. Sol couldn't just make more Exaltations because of the Law of Diminishment, and he had no desire to after seeing what the Solars did to Creation.<br /> <br /> But now he's been given a second chance, as Deathknights blight the land with a dark and twisted spark of his power, in a world lavished by the Contagion and diminished by the Terrestrials, with no Empress to bring law. Sol likely sees the Time of Tulmult as an oppertunity, and a duty, and a penance (for both himself and his Chosen).</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't asking why didn't he make more. I am asking that if all the Solars outside the Jade Prison had already been chosen, and someone else caught the Sun's attention, could he contest its power and pull another one out. In effect, was he unable to chose more than the handful of Solars who weren't caught, or did he not try?<br /> <br /> I am aware that his inner thoughts are even less likely to appear on 3E pages than excerpts from the Jade Prison's user manual. But since the point of this thread is about the morality of his actions, it is relevant to know what he could do vs what he did do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 03-17-2020, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T09:35:42-07:00","id":1375290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375285#post1375285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I wasn't asking why didn't he make more. I am asking that if all the Solars outside the Jade Prison had already been chosen, and someone else caught the Sun's attention, could he contest its power and pull another one out. In effect, what he unable to chose more than the handful of Solars who weren't caught, or did he not try?<br /> <br /> I am aware that his inner thoughts are even less likely to appear on 3E pages than excerpts form the Jade Prison's user manual. But since the point of this thread is about the morality of his actions, it is relevant to know what he could do vs what he did do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I absolutely think the answer is &quot;no, he couldn't have Exalted anyone else&quot;.<br /> <br /> There were probably loads of occasions where he didn't use all the Exaltations available to him, thinking no-one was worthy.<br /> <br /> But (as a fan, not a writer or a dev or anyone important) he absolutely could not have pulled Exaltations from the Jade Prison -- they were locked away beyond his power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T11:26:55-07:00","id":1375304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375290#post1375290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I absolutely think the answer is &quot;no, he couldn't have Exalted anyone else&quot;.<br /> <br /> There were probably loads of occasions where he didn't use all the Exaltations available to him, thinking no-one was worthy.<br /> <br /> But (as a fan, not a writer or a dev or anyone important) he absolutely could not have pulled Exaltations from the Jade Prison -- they were locked away beyond his power.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to go in the opposite direction and say that, in dire circumstances, if he wanted to, he could create a new Exaltation. I don't think it would be one from the Jade Prisons (but I'm not opposed to it) or something along those lines, but I think the Unconquered Sun still has the power to create a few last Exaltations. He's just not willing to do so because of the <i>consequences it could have </i>(putting this in italic because it's supposed to be totally mysterious, devastating, and up to the storyteller)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T12:15:41-07:00","id":1375308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375270#post1375270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a side consequence of the idea that the Unconquered Sun would have ultimately stepped in to intervene is that it weakens the significance of the Scarlet Empress saving the world and what she went through to acquire that power. Not gone entirely, sure, but the idea that there was a safety net definitely feels like it diminishes the stakes and consequences. I think that also has implications for how to handle big threats that one might want to introduce in their own game of they're working off an actual text of &quot;there's a point at which the most powerful god will step in&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is, &quot;What would be the <i>consequence </i>of forcing the Sun to step in?&quot;<br /> <br /> Humanity might not care for those consequences, very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T13:00:39-07:00","id":1375316,"title":"","content":"Speaking mostly from 2E info: The Sun has two options if he decides to get personally involved. One is going mano-a-mano against the fey hoards which is unlikely to be particularly effective since he can still only be in one place at a time. (Beating Balor's face into the ground being a useful and enjoyable exceptional). The other is to fire up the daystar and start rains of sunfire. Given how far the Fey had penetrated that would likely leave most of Creation that isn't the Blessed Isle in ashes.<br /> <br /> Between the two extremes, he could deploy the armies and open the stockpiles of Heaven. Gods are more powerful than mortals, but I highly doubt most of them are martially inclined. Having a lot of panicked socialites on the battlefield would do more harm than good. Yu-Shan may be entirely settled, but it also has enormous estates and massively high standards of living and so lots of space for individuals (who aren't living in their office or on their boss' couch). So their armies may be in the millions, but the Fair Folk were an endless hoard that was attacking the entire border of Creation at once and had only gotten more concentrated as they melted a bunch of it.<br /> <br /> With all his Exalts in a box, his only &quot;middle way&quot; option might have been to personally take command of the Heavenly armies, or assign Mars to do so, try to marshal as much of the Elemental and Terrestrial courts as still existed, and try to get the squabbling, panicking Terrestrial Armies to fall into formation.<br /> <br /> It is possible that the Old Realm had more conventional (between personal combat and end the world level) military power than Heaven did. (The Solars did seem to love their doomsday weapons.) The Usurpation depleted or destroy most of that war material, and reduced the Terrestrial population immensely.<br /> <br /> That would not be an enviable position to be in. Three separate forces that had never worked together, the strongest remaining one having not seen combat in 6k years, the other two massively in disarray, and almost no cnc infrastructure.<br /> <br /> Not insurmountable problems, but it looks an awful lot like exactly what was not supposed to happen when the Mandate of Heaven was given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","user":"Exthalion","date":". 03-17-2020, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T17:55:56-07:00","id":1375348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epicurus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is God willing to prevent evil, but not able? Then he is not omnipotent.<br /> <br /> Is he able, but not willing? Then he is malevolent.<br /> <br /> Is he both able and willing? Then whence cometh evil?<br /> <br /> Is he neither able nor willing? Then why call him God?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I read the sun in the first line, willing but not able to prevent [evil of the day]. For this discussion, being the Balorian Crusade. But I enjoy him being unable due to his morality, not his physicality. He made a promise, that Creation was the Exalted's to rule (or misrule). So he held himself back, and would have kept holding himself back, until the Fae breached the Heavenly City. <br /> <br /> The flaw of perfection is a pretty heavy Solar theme - that someone would be so committed to their word that they let genocidal horrors rage before they break it is exactly the kind of extra I want Sol Invictus to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T20:34:59-07:00","id":1375382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epicurus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Is God willing to prevent evil, but not able? Then he is not omnipotent.<br /> <br /> Is he able, but not willing? Then he is malevolent.<br /> <br /> Is he both able and willing? Then whence cometh evil?<br /> <br /> Is he neither able nor willing? Then why call him God?</div> </div> </div> </div>Epicurus' petulant arguments work better for the Unconquered Sun, who is neither omnipotent or purely good, than they do for God.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun didn't create humanity, nor reality, and thus cannot be a perfect moral arbiter for either.<br /> <br /> He didn't grant humanity free will. Though one could make the argument that he did the next best thing by giving them Exaltation and ownership of Creation, instead of enslaving their species to serve the gods.<br /> <br /> In that sense, he might come close to the idea of a God who granted humanity the freedom to love or reject him. The freedom to defy his will, and go their own way, and to suffer the consequences of doing so.<br /> <br /> Rather like how Creation suffered from the Solar Deliberative, the Usurpation, the Great Contagion, the Fair Folk Invasion, etc.<br /> <br /> But unlike God, the Unconquered Sun isn't allowing these things to happen according to a plan. He doesn't have a perfect afterlife awaiting everyone who obeyed his commands even at the expense of their lives. He isn't planning to eventually end the moral rebellion and set the world back on a harmonious course. He isn't keeping a meticulous record of the crimes of those who, until the end, would rather place themselves before others.<br /> <br /> In the end, the Unconquered Sun is imagined as a man with the powers of a god, rather than a God who designed man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T00:20:01-07:00","id":1375399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375382#post1375382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Epicurus' petulant arguments work better for the Unconquered Sun, who is neither omnipotent or purely good, than they do for God.</div> </div> </div> </div>To the extent that some people claim God is omnipotent and purely good, anyway. Some would disagree with that assertion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T00:46:58-07:00","id":1375401,"title":"","content":"Can we not call people petulant? Or get too into discussing real-world theology.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I prefer to run Exalted's gods like Sunder's last line; not based on current real-world ideas of gods, but rather a person with immense power. I find this works much better.<br /> <br /> Which... admittedly is also why I don't see the need to seriously justify the Sun's decisions, just explain them.<br /> You can just say &quot;he felt X, my PC disagrees&quot;. The UCS felt he couldn't intervene, my PC thinks he was wrong, that's that.<br /> <br /> Although, with the Great Contagion specifically I'm not sure there was anything he could do...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-18-2020, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T01:14:01-07:00","id":1375403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375401#post1375401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we not call people petulant? Or get too into discussing real-world theology.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I prefer to run Exalted's gods like Sunder's last line; not based on current real-world ideas of gods, but rather a person with immense power. I find this works much better.<br /> <br /> Which... admittedly is also why I don't see the need to seriously justify the Sun's decisions, just explain them.<br /> You can just say &quot;he felt X, my PC disagrees&quot;. The UCS felt he couldn't intervene, my PC thinks he was wrong, that's that.<br /> <br /> Although, with the Great Contagion specifically I'm not sure there was anything he could do...</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of wanted to highlight that i agree more or less with all of this. The last sentence esepcially. I get this feeling folks kind of assume the Sun singlehandedly could have pushed back the once-in-all-of-time invasion of the Fair Folk single-handedly, or that untold millions wouldn't have died form the Contagion of all the Solars were around.<br /> <br /> I think in both cases, it kind of is kind of attributing to osme extent too much power to the Sun himself, and the Solar Exalted on their own when the rest of the Exalted Host struggled so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T07:28:13-07:00","id":1375422,"title":"","content":"Also, who is the Unconquerable Sun ? Is he some sort of imitator of the Unconquered Sun, but very noisy, always claiming he could be &quot;Unconquered if he wanted to but no one has ever tried to conquer him, because he is that good, so it's even better but he doesn't care, really&quot; ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T07:28:39-07:00","id":1375423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375401#post1375401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we not call people petulant? Or get too into discussing real-world theology.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was admittedly a little petulant of me, born of the frustration of someone taking a potshot at God in a venue where DEMONSTRABLY any response would provoke &quot;no theological discussion please!&quot; despite the thread being about the morality of gods that rule the universe.<br /> <br /> Do you see anyone taking shots at atheism?<br /> <br /> <br /> But yes, in a game written by people, limited to the imaginations of people, gods must ultimately be envisioned as little different from humans, if humans were in their circumstances.<br /> <br /> Even to the extent that a creature is inhuman, it must still be comprehensibly a creature. Its motives would include self-preservation, often including perpetuation of itself or species through some form of reproduction. It can seem incomprehensible to the extent that the people encountering it do not understand its language, customs, traditions, or the methods and means by which it sustains itself and makes more of its own kind.<br /> <br /> A creature can be made inherently hostile to the extent that its survival depends on preying on humanity exclusively or at least primarily, rather than preying upon easier targets like whales, cows, zebra. Prey that gathers in herds, but that does not have the capacity to organize a counter-offensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T07:28:39-07:00","id":1375424,"title":"","content":"edit: double post","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T07:59:27-07:00","id":1375428,"title":"","content":"Spoilered for off-topic.<br /> \u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375423#post1375423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was admittedly a little petulant of me, born of the frustration of someone taking a potshot at God in a venue where DEMONSTRABLY any response would provoke &quot;no theological discussion please!&quot; despite the thread being about the morality of gods that rule the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Epicurus - to the extent that 3rd-4th-century Christian author Lactantius <i>attributed </i>the problem of evil to him - would have had to take his &quot;potshot&quot; somewhere around 2,300 years ago. Even if this pre-Christian Greek's extant writings <i>did</i> include such a statement (we haven't been able to find it, after all), it wouldn't have been about <i>your </i>guy, because Jesus <i>wasn't born yet</i>.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> \u200bPersonally, I'm of the camp that the more power a being has, the more responsibility it has for the actions it takes - and doesn't take. Since the Sun neither is nor claims to be all-powerful, I'm a lot more willing to be sympathetic as regards <i>his </i>failures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-18-2020, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T08:49:23-07:00","id":1375435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375423#post1375423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was admittedly a little petulant of me, born of the frustration of someone taking a potshot at God in a venue where DEMONSTRABLY any response would provoke &quot;no theological discussion please!&quot; despite the thread being about the morality of gods that rule the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point about no real-world arguments about theology was actually towards Alucard, not you.<br /> Though I realised (I was only skimming) that you were calling Epicurus the philosopher petulant, not a person on this thread! Duh, I feel stupid.<br /> <br /> Still I'm just asking you, Alucard, everyone else, to try and avoid getting too heated in this. (At least, in terms of Christianity, Islam, Buddhism... feel free to argue about the Graeco-Roman Gods.) You want to argue about it by PM of course, go ahead.<br /> <br /> I guess, Alucard, you can do spoilers as you have, but I think the two of you will find it difficult to keep your feelings out of the rest of the thread if you do.<br /> <br /> It is a tricky one; same as when we use political examples or historical examples to compare to Exalted. Exalted is inspired by real-world sources, obviously, and it can be difficult to discuss those without getting into political or religious arguments. I remember this coming up with a point JohnDoe made about Trump for example; it was an interesting point (not one I entirely agreed with, but interesting, but inevitably going to go wrong...<br /> And it can be quite emotive (although some feel it's not emotive enough!) when discussing the Realm and comparing it to real-world Empires.<br /> <br /> I guess just everyone please discuss this with care, sensitivity, and, dare I ironically say it, brotherly/sisterly love?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But yes, in a game written by people, limited to the imaginations of people, gods must ultimately be envisioned as little different from humans, if humans were in their circumstances.<br /> <br /> Even to the extent that a creature is inhuman, it must still be comprehensibly a creature. </div> </div> </div>I generally find that, in practice, running a game, it has to work like this, yeah. Any time PCs meet and discuss things with a deity, Raksha, etc, it's very difficult to do it any other way without seeming... a bit weak. You can do some stuff that's utterly incomprehensible, and not even creature-like or person-like at all, I guess. And simple stuff (animals, for example). Whereas roleplaying a creature that's massively above humanity is very, very difficult. (That's why I'm glad my player who wanted to be Aslan the Lunar went for something else in the end.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T08:52:41-07:00","id":1375437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375270#post1375270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a side consequence of the idea that the Unconquered Sun would have ultimately stepped in to intervene is that it weakens the significance of the Scarlet Empress saving the world and what she went through to acquire that power. Not gone entirely, sure, but the idea that there was a safety net definitely feels like it diminishes the stakes and consequences. I think that also has implications for how to handle big threats that one might want to introduce in their own game of they're working off an actual text of &quot;there's a point at which the most powerful god will step in&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree with this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T08:58:32-07:00","id":1375439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375428#post1375428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the Sun neither is nor claims to be all-powerful, I'm a lot more willing to be sympathetic</div> </div> </div> </div>Ehhhhh... to some extent.<br /> <br /> So going back to my point about what he could and couldn't do.<br /> <br /> He could not have stopped the Great Contagion. If he'd gone down to help humanity, he'd have a chance of dying, possibly pass it on to others, not be able to do anything. Like any great soldier or politician today who went to help with Coronavirus. They might do something, but that's not their skillset.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the case of the Fair Folk, it's a bit more complex. He couldn't wave his hand and wipe them out. But he is a great warrior and general. He could have led the armies of Heaven against them. But, uh... he didn't.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with going &quot;he's a depressed addict, and maybe he was scared, so he just stayed home.&quot; But the original two developers of 3rd ed (who also wrote his entry in Glories, I believe) didn't like that portrayal. They wanted to show him as an extremely virtuous hero. And not going to help when the land is invaded isn't very heroic, is something he could have done, and so then if you want to maintain the idea that he's a good guy, you do need an excuse for him, as Sunder suggests.<br /> <br /> As I said, I don't feel a need to justify his behaviour; I had him killed off in my game anyway because I think he's a very boring character. But if you feel your game could benefit from a heroic and awesome patron for Solars, then one day they may well confront him as to his inaction during the Balorian Crusade, and he'll need a reply.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T10:06:47-07:00","id":1375450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375439#post1375439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhhhh... to some extent.<br /> <br /> So going back to my point about what he could and couldn't do.<br /> <br /> He could not have stopped the Great Contagion. If he'd gone down to help humanity, he'd have a chance of dying, possibly pass it on to others, not be able to do anything. Like any great soldier or politician today who went to help with Coronavirus. They might do something, but that's not their skillset.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the case of the Fair Folk, it's a bit more complex. He couldn't wave his hand and wipe them out. But he is a great warrior and general. He could have led the armies of Heaven against them. But, uh... he didn't.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with going &quot;he's a depressed addict, and maybe he was scared, so he just stayed home.&quot; But the original two developers of 3rd ed (who also wrote his entry in Glories, I believe) didn't like that portrayal. They wanted to show him as an extremely virtuous hero. And not going to help when the land is invaded isn't very heroic, is something he could have done, and so then if you want to maintain the idea that he's a good guy, you do need an excuse for him, as Sunder suggests.<br /> <br /> As I said, I don't feel a need to justify his behaviour; I had him killed off in my game anyway because I think he's a very boring character. But if you feel your game could benefit from a heroic and awesome patron for Solars, then one day they may well confront him as to his inaction during the Balorian Crusade, and he'll need a reply.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>A big thing is the previous devs, to my understnaidng, didn't like he was an addict. They were probably perfectly fine with him being depressed. And despite having written Glories, they were pretty clear it was not how they probably would have written the Sun in 3e, since his 2e take was a response to his depiction up to that point in <i>that edition</i>. 3e was treated by the previous and so far lke the current devs a bit as a soft reboot.<br /> <br /> I think pretty simply, the Sun could simply ahve assessed the situation and thought Heaven wouldn't have changed the tide either way. An invasion on the scale of the Crusade was a once-in-ever occurenc,e and probably somethig nothing in Creation could handle outide of something like the Sword. Maybe the plna as a result was just hunke rdowna nd fight over tha shes for all we know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T19:22:38-07:00","id":1375530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375422#post1375422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, who is the Unconquerable Sun?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the intended humor of you post. I'll add that this is a nice chance to talk about the tense of the Sun's name.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun is not yet conquered, but may be in the future (ambiguous omnipotence). This is the Sol Invictus we know.<br /> <br /> The Unconquerable Sun is unconquered for all time, past, present, and future (explicit omnipotence). Harder moral questions with this one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T19:49:46-07:00","id":1375533,"title":"","content":"The typo was not deliberate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T01:50:48-07:00","id":1375563,"title":"","content":"Unconquerable Sun - I prefer the real Sol<br /> Unconquered Sun - I said the real Sol<br /> Crowned Sun - Perfection","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T01:58:23-07:00","id":1375564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375530#post1375530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the intended humor of you post. I'll add that this is a nice chance to talk about the tense of the Sun's name.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun is not yet conquered, but may be in the future (ambiguous omnipotence). This is the Sol Invictus we know.<br /> <br /> The Unconquerable Sun is unconquered for all time, past, present, and future (explicit omnipotence). Harder moral questions with this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree grammatically (I don't actually know if its a grammar question but I'm not good enough at these) with your explanation, I think that the nature of the names in Exalted are very mythological and contextual (general declared Invincible because they won a huge battle, maidens declared Untainted because they imprisoned dark spirits, etc ...), my joke was focused on the &quot;Unconquerable&quot; being more of an uncertainty (no one has ever tried so who could say the contrary ?) rather than an indisputable definition.<br /> <br /> Who said overexplaining jokes ruined them ?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a> Yes I know I was just teasing and making a joke, didn't mean to offend anyone<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> I get the meme but I don't know the Crowned Sun is that the 1e version or something ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T05:48:59-07:00","id":1375583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375450#post1375450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A big thing is the previous devs, to my understnaidng, didn't like he was an addict. They were probably perfectly fine with him being depressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're probably right. Though I think they were annoyed with the way in which fans had portrayed his addiction at times.<br /> Tbh, I'm not sure anyone really talked explicitly about him being depressed before Vance and Holden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T06:20:35-07:00","id":1375592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375564#post1375564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I get the meme but I don't know the Crowned Sun is that the 1e version or something ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the version of Sol who lost the Primordial War from the Gunstar Shard.<br /> <br /> Has all the Unconquered Sun Charms and all the Malfeas Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T07:11:38-07:00","id":1375600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375592#post1375592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the version of Sol who lost the Primordial War from the Gunstar Shard.<br /> <br /> Has all the Unconquered Sun Charms and all the Malfeas Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh this one seems nasty","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T16:42:58-07:00","id":1375712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375308#post1375308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is, &amp;quot;What would be the <i>consequence </i>of forcing the Sun to step in?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Humanity might not care for those consequences, very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>My imagination genuinely fails me in coming up with such consequences.<br /> <br /> I'll take it as a given that there would be some, but that brings me back around to the feeling that it weakens any given narrative element if it doesn't have stakes for what it is but what will come of the safety net being deployed. I also think there can be problems if consequences take the form of the player characters dealing with more of their significance being ceded from them.<br /> <br /> Blargh, for all that I try to roll back elements of it, the approach to the Unconquered Sun in Glories of the Most High and Ink Monkeys has really done a number on me. Several things might be helped of I could drop this perspective that he's indefatigable and invincible, but I just... can't.<br /> <br /> ... Aaaapart from my idea of how exactly he was Diminished, but that isn't salient to this thread.<br /> <br /> Hmm, speaking of Ink Monkeys, maybe a world governed in accordance to how one of those entries depicted him doling out judgment. Not ready to forgive the Solars yet, but deciding to take a firm hand in getting the other Exalted and the Celestial Order to straighten up and fly right.<br /> <br /> Wait, the topic of this thread is about giving him excuses...<br /> <br /> Suddenly I'm picturing a scenario equivalent to some early strike from the Wyld or consequence of the Contagion bursting a nearby damn, and the Unconquered Sun gets tied in place holding back the wall of water. Maybe something like needing to head down and hold the Kukla in place until his prison stops shaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T16:58:36-07:00","id":1375717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375712#post1375712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Aaaapart from my idea of how exactly he was Diminished, but that isn't salient to this thread.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wait, the topic of this thread is about giving him excuses...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think being Diminished to the point where he really COULDN'T do much of anything to help Creation would be a fine excuse, and perfectly salient to this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T01:47:45-07:00","id":1375770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375308#post1375308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question is, &quot;What would be the <i>consequence </i>of forcing the Sun to step in?&quot;<br /> <br /> Humanity might not care for those consequences, very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>My usual answer to &quot;Let a Great Being come into the field&quot; is usually one of the following :<br /> - He had some sort of duty/watch over something (even if not actively but while he was in Heaven it kept something in check) and this thing has taken the opportunity to f*ck up entirely.<br /> - A being of somewhat equivalent power decides to go into the field as well, maybe not instantly but at a scale and time where it matters to the players (maybe the PC will be on the frontline of the Abyssals/Getiminians/whatever carrying the plan of that being)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":24291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","user":"Chausse","date":". 03-20-2020, 07:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T02:07:32-07:00","id":1375775,"title":"","content":"As a 2-ism...<br /> <br /> What if he just doesn't have free will?<br /> <br /> Like V.I.K.I. from the &quot;I, Robot&quot; film, governed by &quot;programming&quot;, the Sun doesn't have &quot;integrity&quot; (in that he could break his word but doesn't), rather the Sun is physically (and meta-physically) unable to act against his word. Having given Creation to the Exalted, he now can't step in no matter how much it pains him.<br /> <br /> Alternatively/additionally...<br /> <br /> What if the Sun can't intervene but there's an escape clause? If the Exalted fail to defend Creation, then he can take it back.<br /> <br /> Disgusted by the Solars of the First Age, Sol turns his face from Creation, hoping the Solars will redeem themselves. They don't. The Dragon-Blooded usurp them, and (initially) Sol is glad that his trust in humanity isn't misplaced. Then the Shogunate runs the world into the ground. Sol sporadically Exalts his chosen, growing frustrated with humanity. Then the Great Contagion happens, and Sol resolves to take back Creation for himself.<br /> <br /> But he can't, because in theory there's an outside chance that the Exalted might still save Creation. The Solars left behind the Sword of Creation, which might be able to turn the tide. Sol is bound by his word, until the Dragon-Blooded try (and fail) to use the Sword, he has to stay in heaven.<br /> <br /> So he martials his forces, prepares the Aerial Legion for a long hard campaign to drive off the Fair Folk and retake Creation. He also disguises himself as a mortal, Zeus-style, and appears to the greatest Dragon-Blooded heroes to try and prompt them into dropping what they're doing and seeking out the Sword (fully expecting the deadly traps in the Palace of the Anathema to kill them all). The greatest of the Dragon-Blooded heroes brings their girlfriend, a junior officer named Scarlet along.<br /> <br /> Against all odds, the Greatest Dragon-Blooded Hero of All Time actually makes it to the control room of the Sword. Not just Sol, but all of Heaven holds their breath. There is no more Bronze Faction or Gold Faction in that instant. In that moment of glory, humanity has proved its worth, and the Sun is humbled -- all thoughts of going back on his word forgotten. The Dragon-Blooded Hero is a master tactician, and they brilliantly plot an array of tactical strikes against the Fey to destroy the invaders with as little collateral damage as possible... and the Sword reveals one final test. To fire the weapon, the Hero must sacrifice the person they love most. The Hero turns to Scarlet, tears in their eyes, then falls to their knees unable to go through with it.<br /> <br /> Grimly, Sol dons his war helmet and gives the signal for his armies to charge!<br /> <br /> The bravest of the gods hurtle out of Heaven, and are nearly destroyed. The entire sky is aflame! No series of tactical strikes, someone is using the Sword of Creation to utterly scourer the face of Creation with a world-wide carpet-bombing. The Sun frantically looks back to Creation to see the Greatest Dragon-Blooded of All Time murdered without a second's hesitation and Scarlet at the controls doing what needs to be done (her lover's blood still dripping from her hands). Sidereal elders look on with abject horror. The Maidens are unphased -- all is as it should be. The Sun is dumbstruck: this wasn't supposed to happen. The plan was for the Exalted to fail. At worst, the Greatest Dragon-Blooded Ever should have the Weapon.<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Empress has defeated not only the Fey, but the machinations of Heaven. She has conquered love itself and now shoulders the terrible burden of the Creation Ruling Mandate. Her friends are dead. Her lover dead by her hand. Her family destroyed in her opening barrage against the Fey. <br /> <br /> The greatest Sidereal bows before her palace in supplication until she admits him. Sol is fuming. He resolves to take back Creation however he can, and Exalts what champions he deems worthy with the power available to him. But he is neutered. Bound by his word not to interfere in the Exalted's stewardship of Creation. The vast majority of his own Chosen locked away in the Jade Prison. The Sun broods and plays the Games. The Scarlet Empress raises Wyld Hunts against what few Chosen he has.<br /> <br /> The second the Jade Prison opens, Sol turns his face back to the world.<br /> <br /> It is on.<br /> <br /> (Ultimately Sol Invictus is the last boss in the campaign. Everything he does is driven by the knowledge that humanity isn't worthy. What's best for them is if he rules Creation directly with an iron fist. No kindly patron, Sol is an Ozymandias, pragmatic, utilitarian dictator who needs to be proved wrong to save humanity -- whether with logic, noble deeds, trickery or strength of arms. I see a story arc about toppling the Realm, an arc about fighting some unstoppable threat (Yozi, Deathlords, Second Balor, Greater Elemental Dragon) that ends with giving Creation back to Sol, then a story arc about defeating Sol.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-20-2020, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T04:25:25-07:00","id":1375786,"title":"","content":"Huh, that's an original take, making the Sun the last boss. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"dat