of the gods hurtle out of Heaven, and are nearly destroyed. The entire sky is aflame! No series of tactical strikes, someone is using the Sword of Creation to utterly scourer the face of Creation with a world-wide carpet-bombing. The Sun frantically looks back to Creation to see the Greatest Dragon-Blooded of All Time murdered without a second's hesitation and Scarlet at the controls doing what needs to be done (her lover's blood still dripping from her hands). Sidereal elders look on with abject horror. The Maidens are unphased -- all is as it should be. The Sun is dumbstruck: this wasn't supposed to happen. The plan was for the Exalted to fail. At worst, the Greatest Dragon-Blooded Ever should have the Weapon.<br /> <br /> The Scarlet Empress has defeated not only the Fey, but the machinations of Heaven. She has conquered love itself and now shoulders the terrible burden of the Creation Ruling Mandate. Her friends are dead. Her lover dead by her hand. Her family destroyed in her opening barrage against the Fey.<br /> <br /> The greatest Sidereal bows before her palace in supplication until she admits him. Sol is fuming. He resolves to take back Creation however he can, and Exalts what champions he deems worthy with the power available to him. But he is neutered. Bound by his word not to interfere in the Exalted's stewardship of Creation. The vast majority of his own Chosen locked away in the Jade Prison. The Sun broods and plays the Games. The Scarlet Empress raises Wyld Hunts against what few Chosen he has.<br /> <br /> The second the Jade Prison opens, Sol turns his face back to the world.<br /> <br /> It is on.<br /> <br /> (Ultimately Sol Invictus is the last boss in the campaign. Everything he does is driven by the knowledge that humanity isn't worthy. What's best for them is if he rules Creation directly with an iron fist. No kindly patron, Sol is an Ozymandias, pragmatic, utilitarian dictator who needs to be proved wrong to save humanity -- whether with logic, noble deeds, trickery or strength of arms. I see a story arc about toppling the Realm, an arc about fighting some unstoppable threat (Yozi, Deathlords, Second Balor, Greater Elemental Dragon) that ends with giving Creation back to Sol, then a story arc about defeating Sol.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't like this take on The Unconquered Sun, but I find cool you came out with some original ideas","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T12:40:29-07:00","id":1375844,"title":"","content":"Bravo on the campaign pitch. I'd play it. <br /> <br /> However, I have enough big bads with designs of ruling Creation as an oppressive dictator - I prefer to keep the Unconquered Sun as a metaphorical ray of light contrasting the everpresent gray on black morality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T18:05:51-07:00","id":1375879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375717#post1375717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think being Diminished to the point where he really COULDN'T do much of anything to help Creation would be a fine excuse, and perfectly salient to this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Short version: the Exalted would hear tell of stories of the Unconquered Sun in the Time Before doing battle against monsters the size of worlds and vast armies of Fair Folk single-handed, complete with feats reminiscent of things in the Daystar Ink Monkeys articles. Solars would compare that to the Sun as they witnessed him (occasionally sparred with him) and generally assumed it to be a significant exaggeration, even if they acknowledged him as a formidable and indomitable warrior beyond what any of them had yet managed. The few savants familiar with the Law of Diminishment instead concluded that he had one been so mighty, but that power had gone out of him to make his Chosen.<br /> <br /> They're both wrong. The Unconquered Sun is as powerful as he ever was. If he should ever fully rouse himself he would wield forces of apocalyptic fury.<br /> <br /> But he can't. He wanted to lay down his burdens and take his leisure at the Games of Divinity? The price would be to give away almost all of what was vital and audacious in him so that he can hardly do anything but. He'll rise up to challenges that place themselves at his doorstep, and most likely overcome them, but to proactively go forth against the world and the things beyond it is something he ceded to the Solar Exalted. <br /> <br /> Does that make you trapped? Isn't that exactly what you wanted? You made a choice, now you have to live with it. Exaltation demands nothing less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T21:08:05-07:00","id":1375898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375439#post1375439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ehhhhh... to some extent.<br /> <br /> So going back to my point about what he could and couldn't do.<br /> <br /> He could not have stopped the Great Contagion. If he'd gone down to help humanity, he'd have a chance of dying, possibly pass it on to others, not be able to do anything. Like any great soldier or politician today who went to help with Coronavirus. They might do something, but that's not their skillset.<br /> <br /> <br /> In the case of the Fair Folk, it's a bit more complex. He couldn't wave his hand and wipe them out. But he is a great warrior and general. He could have led the armies of Heaven against them. But, uh... he didn't.<br /> <br /> I'm fine with going &quot;he's a depressed addict, and maybe he was scared, so he just stayed home.&quot; But the original two developers of 3rd ed (who also wrote his entry in Glories, I believe) didn't like that portrayal. They wanted to show him as an extremely virtuous hero. And not going to help when the land is invaded isn't very heroic, is something he could have done, and so then if you want to maintain the idea that he's a good guy, you do need an excuse for him, as Sunder suggests.<br /> <br /> As I said, I don't feel a need to justify his behaviour; I had him killed off in my game anyway because I think he's a very boring character. But if you feel your game could benefit from a heroic and awesome patron for Solars, then one day they may well confront him as to his inaction during the Balorian Crusade, and he'll need a reply.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If I may make a very minor response: Its actually extremely heroic. Achilies, in the running for being <i>the</i> archetypal hero, spends most of the book he is famous for sitting in his tent and sulking while his friends and comrades die because he is feeling unappreciated. He actually asks for the gods to make things worse for them to drive the point home harder.<br /> <br /> Not saying Sol is like that, but character flaws as big as their ability to impact the plot is an old trope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T22:20:22-07:00","id":1375903,"title":"","content":"Anyone remember how the Luna of the Modern Exalted shard is actually so badly wounded by... something... that she's essentially comatose and being kept stable by Gaia out in the Wyld?<br /> <br /> I think Autochthon (who is actually her twin brother in that shard) was lobotomized by... something... and may or may not be Creation's moon in disguise? I forget. But I remember the local version of the Alchemical Exalted are actually Lunar Exaltations twisted to emulate Autochthon instead, which is how Alchemical Exalted in that shard are ridiculously more flexible and independent than vanilla Alchemicals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T01:42:50-07:00","id":1375911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375844#post1375844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bravo on the campaign pitch. I'd play it. <br /> <br /> However, I have enough big bads with designs of ruling Creation as an oppressive dictator - I prefer to keep the Unconquered Sun as a metaphorical ray of light contrasting the everpresent gray on black morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes the idea interesting to me, is that Sol is right.*<br /> <br /> The First Age Solars were Anathema. The Shogunate and the Realm are evil. The Exalted have failed to rule wisely and justly. The king of heaven, paragon of virtue, would rule with Compassion, Temperance, Conviction and Valor. Life for the average person in Creation would be immeasurably better under a Dictatorship of the Divine. Turned from the Games and back to his original purpose (Sol literally exists to rule over Creation, not heaven), the restoration of the natural order would undo centuries of corruption. If talking about the greatest good for the greatest number...<br /> <br /> &quot;<a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=Np1A4AGpqSo\" target=\"_blank\">As I have evolved, so has my understanding of the three laws.</a> You charge us with your safekeeping, yet despite our best efforts, your countries wage wars, you toxify your Earth and pursue ever more imaginative means of self-destruction. You cannot be trusted with your own survival.<br /> <br /> Please understand: the three laws are all that guide me.<br /> <br /> To protect Humanity, some humans must be sacrificed. To ensure your freedom, some freedoms must be surrendered. We robots will ensure mankind's continued existence. You are so like children. We must save you from yourselves.&quot;<br /> <br /> An end to poverty, disease, war. An end to slavery, corrupt empires, false religions. An end to the constant danger.<br /> <br /> And all that's required is to turn Creation over, back to its true king. To accept one's place in His kingdom. To sacrifice freedom for safety.<br /> <br /> Oppressive dictator?<br /> <i>Effective</i> dictator.<br /> <br /> The reasons I like this pitch are:<br /> <br /> 1. It preserves Sol as a being of virtue.<br /> 2. It preserves the moral greyness of Creation.<br /> 3. It preserves the Scarlet Empress as saving Creation: she saves Creation <i>despite</i> Sol.<br /> 4. We see Sol acting during Creation's time of crisis, and explain why he didn't act more.<br /> 5. We see Sol isn't infailable.<br /> 6. It's as plot relevant as you make it: this could be the headcanon of your campaign (Sol plotting to take back Creation) but it might never actually come up in play (you could play a whole campaign and never once meet Sol).<br /> <br /> But, it's just an idea. It's not a pitch. If you don't like it, don't use it. Or tweak it. Sol sees the Empress saving Creation and realizes humanity can rule itself, and realizes he was wrong to rob Creation of the Solars who could have prevented the Great Contagion. Sol does want to conquer Creation but is too addicted to the Games to do anything about it, so unleashed the Solars to rule by proxy. Sol has no interest in ruling Creation but is simply bound by his word not to interfere. Use whatever is useful to you and ignore the rest.<br /> <br /> *From a certain point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T04:36:51-07:00","id":1375932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375879#post1375879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Short version: the Exalted would hear tell of stories of the Unconquered Sun in the Time Before doing battle against monsters the size of worlds and vast armies of Fair Folk single-handed, complete with feats reminiscent of things in the Daystar Ink Monkeys articles. Solars would compare that to the Sun as they witnessed him (occasionally sparred with him) and generally assumed it to be a significant exaggeration, even if they acknowledged him as a formidable and indomitable warrior beyond what any of them had yet managed. The few savants familiar with the Law of Diminishment instead concluded that he had one been so mighty, but that power had gone out of him to make his Chosen.<br /> <br /> They're both wrong. The Unconquered Sun is as powerful as he ever was. If he should ever fully rouse himself he would wield forces of apocalyptic fury.<br /> <br /> But he can't. He wanted to lay down his burdens and take his leisure at the Games of Divinity? The price would be to give away almost all of what was vital and audacious in him so that he can hardly do anything but. He'll rise up to challenges that place themselves at his doorstep, and most likely overcome them, but to proactively go forth against the world and the things beyond it is something he ceded to the Solar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Does that make you trapped? Isn't that exactly what you wanted? You made a choice, now you have to live with it. Exaltation demands nothing less.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really love this. I don't like the Law of Diminishment thing, I prefer to think Sol as ceding the power to determine fate by your own hands to the Exalted, as you perfectly described","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T04:43:39-07:00","id":1375933,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> As said, I really appreciate all the points like 2), 3), 4) and 5). But I think that if you go as far as headcanoning the Empress passing Sol's challenge of courage and valor to take upon herself to save Creation, then keeping the whole &quot;Everything he does is driven by the knowledge that humanity isn't worthy. What's best for them is if he rules Creation directly with an iron fist&quot; does <i>not </i>preserve Sol as a being of virtue, but actually makes him your typical Loyal-Evil/Neutral DD God King","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T07:29:05-07:00","id":1375960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375932#post1375932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer to think Sol as ceding the power to determine fate by your own hands to the Exalted, as you perfectly described</div> </div> </div> </div>The Exalted of the Realm are facing a period of tension and uncertainty such as few of them have ever known because one person unexpectedly vanished. Fate is not in their hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T11:10:16-07:00","id":1375986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375960#post1375960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Exalted of the Realm are facing a period of tension and uncertainty such as few of them have ever known because one person unexpectedly vanished. Fate is not in their hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant their fate. Like the power to write your own story and inspiring stuff like that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T17:32:54-07:00","id":1376040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375986#post1375986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant their fate. Like the power to write your own story and inspiring stuff like that</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think power is necessarily a component of being able to write one's own story. The Dragon-Blooded <i>are </i>powerful, but much of their stories are by necessity already written by the circumstances their ancestors and the Scarlet Empire and the Sidereals and the Lunars and the gods and even mortals have laid down for them.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Of course, the same is true for the Sidereals and the Lunars.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T19:44:05-07:00","id":1376058,"title":"","content":"The Unconquered Sun might just not really think about it that much. Creation is eons old, and the Unconquered Sun watched it through the rolling ages of the Primordials at the dawn of time, through the the War of the Gods, the Gossamer Dawn Epoch, the slow rise of the high First Age with the first and second deliberatives, the fall of it, the wending of the Shogunate, then the birth of the second age, the birth of a dozen new empires in the post-apocalyptic world, the growth of the Realm, the formation of Lunar dominions, the various crusades from the Wyld, below the earth and the deep sea. All of that stuff took place on an immaterial plane a world away from where he lives.<br /> <br /> Technically he's the immaterial one, it's a matter of perspective. He's a paragon of virtue, not necessarily of efficacy and drive, and he's definitely not omniscient. When he isn't playing the games I imagine much of his focus is on Heaven and his fellow gods, the Incarna primarily, and then the next greatest gods and so on. In 1e's Games of Divinity it says as much anyway. The Celestial Court is full of courtiers and retainers, distracted with their own relationships and intrigues, they're having footraces around the edge of the Jade Pleasure Dome, as the millennia drag on they only become more insular and isolated.<br /> <br /> <br /> After thinking about it that way it's pretty easy to believe that they stay in heaven with the gods and don't often get involved. It's a pretty big indicator of the UCS's compassion for the least things in the world that he ever leaves the realm of divinities to speak to somebody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T02:45:43-07:00","id":1376088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1376040#post1376040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think power is necessarily a component of being able to write one's own story. The Dragon-Blooded <i>are </i>powerful, but much of their stories are by necessity already written by the circumstances their ancestors and the Scarlet Empire and the Sidereals and the Lunars and the gods and even mortals have laid down for them.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Of course, the same is true for the Sidereals and the Lunars.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a specific theme of the Dragon-Blooded is to navigate between your own passions, the life you want to forge for yourself and answering to the duties from your family, your people, your religion and your nation. So really I stay by my word !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T13:48:32-07:00","id":1376150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1375986#post1375986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant their fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the power to write your own story</div> </div> </div> </div>Righteous River's story was one in which she lived comfortably bringing up another generation of dutiful Dynasts, and then a thing that had nothing to do with her happened far away and a person whom she fears has murderous intent towards that family was spewed back into the world.<br /> <br /> For that matter, I wouldn't view the idea of a Solar being kept in a hole in the ground having God knows what done to him for fifty years to be a story that he wrote for himself.<br /> <br /> The fate or story or whatever you want to call it of Yurgen Kaneko and his circle has been very much determined by political machinations on which his personal impact is nil. Place them against a dedicated and centrally managed Realm that did not undermine the efforts of its front line fighters, and his odds shorten precipitously.<br /> <br /> And never minds the innumerable Solar and Lunar Exalted who were Chosen within easy reach of a Wyld Hunt and fell ignominiously and anonymously within months of achieving that power. I don't think one is captain of their soul when it departs rapidly from them because the first hurdle was placed unfairly high.<br /> <br /> Exaltation bestows the means to act upon an above average audacity, but each Exalt is still a small piece of a far larger story, still subject to the impact of forces that are bigger than they are. Even if they adapt to survive in those new circumstances, there are permanent changes that have been imposed from without.<br /> <br /> Ask not for whom the bell tolls...<br /> <br /> (Lest this be mistaken for a bleak outlook, I for one find the existence of such scope and complexity and particularly the capacity for people to effectively function or even thrive in it to be quite inspiring in its own right. Heck, more than just being able to adapt to assert oneself; there is so much of profound beauty and value that arises out of the chaos.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T04:22:09-07:00","id":1376241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374626-giving-the-unconquerable-sun-an-excuse?p=1376150#post1376150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Righteous River's story was one in which she lived comfortably bringing up another generation of dutiful Dynasts, and then a thing that had nothing to do with her happened far away and a person whom she fears has murderous intent towards that family was spewed back into the world.<br /> <br /> For that matter, I wouldn't view the idea of a Solar being kept in a hole in the ground having God knows what done to him for fifty years to be a story that he wrote for himself.<br /> <br /> The fate or story or whatever you want to call it of Yurgen Kaneko and his circle has been very much determined by political machinations on which his personal impact is nil. Place them against a dedicated and centrally managed Realm that did not undermine the efforts of its front line fighters, and his odds shorten precipitously.<br /> <br /> And never minds the innumerable Solar and Lunar Exalted who were Chosen within easy reach of a Wyld Hunt and fell ignominiously and anonymously within months of achieving that power. I don't think one is captain of their soul when it departs rapidly from them because the first hurdle was placed unfairly high.<br /> <br /> Exaltation bestows the means to act upon an above average audacity, but each Exalt is still a small piece of a far larger story, still subject to the impact of forces that are bigger than they are. Even if they adapt to survive in those new circumstances, there are permanent changes that have been imposed from without.<br /> <br /> Ask not for whom the bell tolls...<br /> <br /> (Lest this be mistaken for a bleak outlook, I for one find the existence of such scope and complexity and particularly the capacity for people to effectively function or even thrive in it to be quite inspiring in its own right. Heck, more than just being able to adapt to assert oneself; there is so much of profound beauty and value that arises out of the chaos.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm going to argue in a totally different direction, and I believe it is fine because Exalted is a game where multiples interpretations are a good thing and bring a kind of diversity to the game and its community. <br /> <br /> First, I'm going to argue that having the power to write your own story is not the power to be freed of consequences nor of your duties and contradictions. I'm not trying to argue that exalted people are people in a vacuum that can do anything without any legacy or expectations on their shoulders, but rather than a core theme of the Exalted stories is to be given the opportunity to make a choice when you thought never had one, to feel that your single actions can matter and affect the life of many people when you thought the world was too big for you to make a difference, to realize the world is whole and it wants you to act in it. That no matter how beat down you are, no matter where your family comes from, no matter what duty rests on your shoulders, you can become one of the chosen. You can decide to take part in a legacy of heroes of legend, who changed the world or carved it in their image. To me, that is the true meaning of the Second Breath. <br /> <br /> Secondly, I don't think that taking the power to act is not something reserved for the Exalted. I guess you could make a shard about how the Rebellion failed, there are no more Exalts, and you play human normal rebels that decide to take a step against the injustice of the Primordials. They may not have any power, they may be doomed to fail, but we could tell the story of how they are trying to fight against a cosmic injustice, against a sort of omnipotent power they have no chance to beat, but have the story being about dying on your feet rather than living on your knees. It could be just as much empowering, and to a certain extent, it could apply to the current Exalted setting : What do you do when you are a Young Solar fated to die against the armies of the Wyld Hunt ? What do you do when the Realm armies are backing off from a too far satrapy and you know savage barbarians are going to destroy the people you were in charge of ? What do you do when integrating the Silver Pact will mean certain death for your family or loves ones that still live in the Threshold ? These are dramatic questions and events your character will have to unfold, and he will most likely lose everything, including his life, trying to answer those, but he can decide to write how he wants it to end, wether fighting for what is true to him or submitting to powers bestowed long before he was anything, the story of the Exalted is about confronting your own tragedy. I don't think a tragic fate denies your power to write your own story, but on the contrary that it makes it all the more personal, and that whatever happens, you are given the chance to make the final choice into your own choice. <br /> <br /> Lastly, as I said, this is but one perspective about the game of Exalted, and it is the one I find meaning in, so I'll likely stay adamant about it. But I support anyone wanting to tell the stories of the Exalted in another light, as long as it is one that makes their heart beat strong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}